Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in collaboration with its consortium partners, proposes a comprehensive solution for the City of Belval's artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool. Our approach integrates AI innovation, security compliance, legal adherence, budget optimization, and sustainability principles to deliver an effective, transparent, and environmentally responsible system. We leverage our expertise in Agile Scrum methodology, sovereign cloud hosting, GDPR compliance, and green IT practices to ensure a tailored solution that meets the City's specific needs.

### Understanding of Requirements
The City of Belval requires an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents in their daily missions, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. The solution must integrate with existing systems, respect regulatory requirements (notably GDPR), ensure data sovereignty, and minimize environmental impact. Key functionalities include assistance with information consultation, drafting, file instruction, and collaboration.

### Proposed Solution
Our proposed solution utilizes the Mistral 7B Instruct LLM model for strong French-language performance, combined with RAG capabilities for accurate information retrieval from the city's knowledge base. We apply fine-tuning methods like LoRA or full fine-tune on a domain-specific corpus to adapt the model to the city's tone and format requirements, aiming for an average accuracy gain of 12%. For explicability and transparency, we implement XAI methods including source citation through RAG grounding, chain-of-thought display, and confidence scoring, with a low-confidence threshold set at 0.65.

To ensure seamless integration, we use API gateways like Kong, message brokers like Apache Kafka, and identity providers like Active Directory / LDAP or Keycloak. Our hosting solution leverages Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud, European suppliers that meet the sovereignty requirement, with a PUE rating of 1.3 and 1.28, respectively. We design a cloud-native architecture utilizing containerisation with Docker, Kubernetes (K8s), and Helm for efficient deployment and management.

Our security posture is grounded in our ISO 27001 certification and GDPR compliance, with standard data residency in the EU, cross-border transfer policy, and utilization of anonymisation tools like Microsoft Presidio. We perform Data Protection Impact Assessments (DPIAs) within an average duration of 3 weeks and emphasize AI security controls including prompt injection protection, output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, confidence threshold escalation, model isolation, and the security review process for model updates.

From a legal perspective, we highlight our standard legal basis under Article 6(1)(e) of the GDPR for processing personal data and adherence to the EU AI Act, ensuring transparency and human oversight in our solution. Our default IP model transfers all deliverables to the client upon final payment, and we offer source code escrow capability through Logitas (France).

While specific cost details are not provided due to lack of information on project expenses, our general approach to budget optimization includes absorbing costs via rate renegotiation with subcontractors for up to a 10% reduction and scope reduction by removing optional modules and reducing training days for up to a 20% reduction.

In terms of sustainability, we propose leveraging green hosting partners OVHcloud and Scaleway, both powered by 100% renewable energy. Our digital sobriety practices aim to reduce energy consumption by an estimated 35%, including INT8/INT4 model quantisation, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy.

### Unaddressed Requirements
Due to the lack of specific cost information related to the project, we cannot provide detailed financial projections or exact costs for our proposed solution. However, we emphasize our commitment to transparency and are prepared to work closely with the City of Belval to develop a comprehensive and tailored budget plan upon receipt of more detailed project requirements.

### Conclusion
Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with its consortium partners, is committed to delivering an innovative, secure, compliant, and sustainable artificial intelligence solution for the City of Belval. Our approach combines cutting-edge technologies with robust methodologies to ensure the development of a tool that not only meets but exceeds the city's expectations for assisting municipal agents in their daily activities. We look forward to the opportunity to collaborate closely with the City of Belval to tailor our proposal further and address any additional requirements or concerns that may arise during the project's development.
